rmed by  three other small strips of land abdal  kuri darsa and sama the six thousand  inhabitants living on the island have  always relied on fishing and on the  cultivation of date poems and despite  belonging politically to yemen since  1999 the islanders half shiite and half  sonny boast their own culture and a  different language sokotri a semitic  language even older than arabic and  whose origin is still an arcane mystery  up to this day socotra find itself  embroiled in a civil war that has been  ravaging yemen since 2015. sokotra  became the epicenter of a power struggle  between the houthi rebels and the  central government but it became also  the place of another secondary conflict  the one between the united arab emirates  and the yemeni government of mansur hadi  the situation in yemen has been tragic  for over six years to be exact since  hadi was forced by shiite rebels  belonging to the ansar allah group  better known as houthi to resign from  its presidency abandon the capital sena  and leave it under the control of the  rebels the war in yemen is better known  as a proxy war a conflict where the real  actors are quite different from those  facing each other on the battlefield  under the surface yemen is actually  disputed on one side by the saudis  supported by the rest of the gulf  countries and the us which approved the  official government of adi and on the  other side there's iran which in  historical contrast to the saudi  monarchy supports the rebellion of the  houthis seeing it is as a possibility to  expand the sphere of influence directly  in the arabian peninsula we'll talk more  about the war in yemen in another video  this is not the case i'll just focus now  on socotra known as the jewel of the  gulf of aden sokotra is situated off the  horn of africa overlooking the baba  mondeb strait which connects the red sea  to both the gulf of aden and the arabian  sea the tensions surrounding socotra are  many every day more than 3 million oil  barrels travel from the persian gulf to  the indian ocean ships on this route  travel west across the arabian sea into  the gulf of aden then turn north  entering the red sea through the narrow  babel mandel passage before going up to  the suez canal the socotra archipelago  occupies a critical position on the  route to babel mondeb zakotra's central  location also makes it an ideal  launching point for interdicting pirates  and smugglers it protects the trade  routes and all the fishing communities  along the horn of africa and the  southern coast of yemen from iran to  somalia and from eritrea to qatar in  india for years international regional  powers have struggled to establish bases  around the horn of africa to have a  strategic advantage over all these  nations are the united arab emirates  which since 2018 have maintained a  military presence on the island to  support the cts which is the southern  transitional council an entity whose  purpose is to achieve the separation of  south yemen from the rest of the nation  the emirates presence though has only  increased divisions on the island  sokotra's governor ramsey marus has  always rejected the presence of the cts  being in his eyes a clear threat to his  figure on the other hand however many  islanders are polarized on the choice to  adapt to support the transnational  council of the south and therefore the  arab emirates or to refuse the  interference of a foreign country in the  island's affairs separated from food and  fuel supplies since the outbreak of the  war the island was left at the mercy of  its own fate the absence of huti on the  island couldn't grant a kazoo's belly to  intervene militarily and so the emirates  with the initial support of the saudis  used the excuse of humanitarian aid to  set foot on the island and secure the  support of part of the population they  found the opportunity in 2015 when in  the space of a few days socotra ended up  being hit by two tropical cyclones that  brought destruction and further misery  to the population that had already been  living on less than one dollar a day for  decades masquerading it as a large-scale  humanitarian intervention by the red  crescent abu dhabi deployed over 5 000  troops to the island without the  coordination or approval of either the  yemeni government or the governor of  socotra in 2018 the united arab emirates  under the guise of training local yemeni  forces in socotra reportedly began to  weave a series of personal interests on  the island first of all they did it to  strengthen military connection with all  their bases along the horn of africa  such as the berbera base and somaliland  the assab noble base in eritrea and  other military barracks in pontland in  somalia from a strategic point of view  socotra provides a vital link between  these regions and would allow the  emirate navi to conduct important  security operations in terms of  contrasting piracy the island has long  been a docking base for many of the  somali pirates who operate far and wide  along the horn of africa as far as the  omani coast a stable presence would also  allow the emirates and implicitly the  saudis to keep out iranian boats that  transport arms and supplies to the  houthi rebels in a proxy war against  iran all of this would strengthen saudi  arabia in this conflict socotra would  serve as an excellent support base from  which to launch rockets against the  houthis in yemen the news that the  emirates used socultura as a military  base is still a matter of debate given  the logistical problems of the island  such as those dictated by the climate  and by monsoons which for six months of  the year make operations in the era very  difficult the interest of the united  arab emirates in socotra has been  interpreted as a challenge by saudi  arabia by occupying the island the  emirates are trying to block the  expansion and the regional domination of  saudi arabia in the entire region  consolidating their presence in the  triangle that at its vertices touches  aidan socotra and the small island of  barim and so the reasons that led abu  dhabi to be guaranteed a 99-year  concession by president hadi would be  mainly economic controlling socra would  mean acquiring a large slice of the  monopoly in the traffic of oil and gas  that passes through babel mandeb a move  made in total autonomy and in contrast  with both iran and saudi arabia with the  occupation of socotra the emirates would  also be able to acquire kilometers and  kilometers of indian ocean through the  strengthening of an exclusive economic  zone in the territorial waters around  the island for the saudis the emirates  are an alliance of convenience it's not  by chance that the emirates are planning  to annex socotra by organizing a  referendum in order to make the  islanders decide whether to become  officially part of the emirates or  remain at the mercy of the uncertainty  of war feeling neglected by hadi's  central government the sokotrians had no  choice but to welcome abu dhabi's  investments the emiratis have not only  built basic infrastructures such as  roads hospitals and schools but also  paid the salaries of doctors policemen  and bureaucrats creating new  opportunities for a total of five  thousand new jobs after two weeks in may  2018 the emirati troops abandoned the  island they got replaced by saudi troops  but they still left behind officials who  are working for the khalifa foundation  of abu dhabi a government-sponsored  charity for governor marusa however such  charitable organizations would conceal a  more devious objective that is to buy  the loyalty of socotra residents and  allow uai traders and investors to  conduct business on the island under  their cover these organizations would  facilitate the purchase of land to  wealthy emiratis despite the presence of  a government decree prohibiting the sale  of any land on the island many of these  lots would belong to protected coastal  areas in which the construction of  buildings and changes to the landscapes  are prohibited yet when buying land with  prices ranging from hundreds of  thousands to tens of millions of dollars  emiratis have never hidden their goals  of building private houses and tourist  resorts emirates and no longer yemen  seem to have become the headquarters of  the island witness to these are the  emirati companies which have weekly  flights between hadibu the capital of  socotra and abu dhabi the united arab  emirates are also aware that socotra may  become a great catalyst for tourism  before the civil war the island operated  a particular kind of ecotourism  respectful of the environment which  granted a small number of visas per year  especially to scientists to facilitate  their study of social ecosystem all of  these may disappear with the emirati  occupation and with their plans to favor  luxury resorts all over the island just  like they already did in dubai with  their artificial archipelagos i dare to  say that the objective is very simple to  transform socotra into a dubai 2.0 to do  so socotra's deputy governor for  environment and development abdul jameel  mohammed as well as emirati companies  have reportedly already begun excavating  several sections of the island's  national park in preparation for a  series of five-star resorts leaving  aside the contradictions of seeing  five-star hotels in villages still  destroyed by monsoons and poverty all of  this has raised a lot of criticism in  the island as reported by local sources  the emirates didn't obtain any  permission from yemen to start their  construction projects in addition to  this some reports highlighted that  several endangered species both plants  and animals have been taken from the  island and resettled into the emirates  many soccotians saw this move as not  only a violation of the island's  identity but also as an offense against  their environment something made  possible by the position of supremacy  enjoyed by emirati officials there the  possibility of the island being used as  a new destination for vacationing has  raised concerns related to pollution of  a fragile ecosystem and maybe this is  the saddest element of the story also  the fact that the emirates several  months later send troops on the island  again  doesn't bode well abu dhabi doesn't seem  willing to leave the bone which is  metaphorically the island in the hands  of the saudis for this is what's all  about a bone an island that's at risk of  being stripped of its beauty for mere  geopolitical and economic plots yemeni  journalist muhammad al-rumeem earlier  this year said the united arab emirates  are not a friend of socotra they're only  interested in colonizing it the emirates  have always denied the accusation of  neo-colonialism but what seems more and  more certain is that the emiratis intend  to keep their presence on the island  with or without yemeni approval on the  one hand this allows the emirates to  avoid open conflicts with the arabs and  other competitors such as israel which  seems to have an intelligent space on  the island on the other hand it  relegates the islanders to  mere pawns in a geopolitical chess game  whose outcome could prove catastrophic  for their traditional lifestyle and also  for the island they call home only time  will tell us which side will prevail  they say however that time is a  gentleman but i have serious doubts that  it will be so in this case i thank all  of you for listening and keeping me  company until the end see you in the  next video bye

